{"shortDescription":"By Vedika ThoratUS natural gas futures fell more than 3% on Monday as forecasts for milder temperatures and lower oil prices weighed on the market after weeks of weather-driven strength.Front-month gas futures NYMEX:NG1! for October delivery on the New York Mercantile Exchange settled down by 7.6 c…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Vedika Thorat"]},{"type":"p","children":["US natural gas futures fell more than 3% on Monday as forecasts for milder temperatures and lower oil prices weighed on the market after weeks of weather-driven strength."]},{"type":"p","children":["Front-month gas futures ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NYMEX:NG1!","text":"NYMEX:NG1!"}}," for October delivery on the New York Mercantile Exchange settled down by 7.6 cents, or 2.6%, at $2.836 per million British thermal units."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"The weather has moderated. And typically, for natural gas, weather plays a key role, especially short-term. And so with the moderating weather, moderating temperatures, the market is moving off a little bit here,\" said Thomas Saal, senior vice president at StoneX."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meteorologists forecast weather would remain mostly warmer than normal through October 4."]},{"type":"p","children":["Financial firm LSEG said average gas output in the US Lower 48 states rose to 113.1 billion cubic feet per day (bcfd) so far in September, up from a monthly record high of 112.2 bcfd in August."]},{"type":"p","children":["LSEG said average gas demand in the Lower 48 states, including exports, is expected to slide from 107.6 bcfd this week to 104.8 bcfd next week."]},{"type":"p","children":["Analysts predicted the amount of gas in storage slid to 2.9% above normal during the week ended September 18, down from 3.7% above normal in the previous week, according to early estimates ahead of Thursday's weekly federal inventory report."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, oil prices slid towards the psychological threshold of $100 a barrel and to their lowest in 11 days as investors hoped for diplomatic progress on the Iran war due to this week's United Nations meeting, and eyed a partial recovery in shipments from Saudi Arabia."]},{"type":"p","children":["Average gas flows to the nine big US LNG export plants rose to 18.1 bcfd so far in September, up from 17.2 bcfd in August, but remained short of the monthly record high of 18.8 bcfd in April."]},{"type":"p","children":["Dutch and British gas prices fell, also on hopes of progress on the Iran conflict, and with temperatures expected to be unseasonally mild next week."]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Week ended Sep 18 Forecast"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Week ended  Sep 11 Actual"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Year ago Sep 18"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Five-year average (2021-2025) Sep 18"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["US weekly natgas storage change (bcf):"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+51"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+44"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+77"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+76"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["US total natgas in storage (bcf):"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3,349"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3,298"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"t